# Matrix shape, products, transpose, determinant, inverse, and identity.
A as Matrix[Float, 2, 2] is [[1.0, 2.0], [3.0, 4.0]]
B as Matrix[Float, 2, 2] is [[5.0, 6.0], [7.0, 8.0]]
x as Vector[Float, 2] is [5.0, 6.0]
rhs as Matrix[Float, 2, 2] is [[5.0, 2.0], [5.0, 1.0]]

Sayln shape(A)
Sayln trace(A)
Sayln rank(A)
Sayln multiply(A, B)
Sayln matvec(A, x)
Sayln transpose(A)
Sayln multiply(A, identity(2))
Sayln determinant(A)
Sayln inverse(A)
Sayln solve(A, [5.0, 11.0])
Sayln solve(A, rhs)
(L, U, P) is lu(A)
Sayln multiply(P, A)
Sayln multiply(L, U)
(Q, R) is qr(A)
Sayln multiply(Q, R)
positive_definite as Matrix[Float, 2, 2] is [[4.0, 2.0], [2.0, 3.0]]
Sayln cholesky(positive_definite)
Sayln least_squares([[1, 0], [0, 1], [1, 1]], [2, 3, 5])
